# Phase 9 Step 4 — Statistical hypothesis tests
Seed: 42, B (bootstrap): 5000
α per test: 0.01 (Bonferroni-corrected family α = 0.006 for family of 8 tests)

## H1 — cross-collection attention non-uniformity
Categorical test: for each collection, what fraction of peaks land on (lesion ∪ skin) vs (vignette ∪ ruler ∪ hair)?

  Contingency (collection × shortcut-vs-not):
spatial_shortcut    0  1
source_collection       
70                 97  3
212                96  4
249                92  8

  χ² = 2.947, dof = 2, p = 0.2291
  H1 supported (p < 0.01)? False

  H1 falsified — attention is uniformly low-shortcut across collections. Note this may reflect peak-IoU threshold strictness rather than absence of shortcut.

## H2 — per-shortcut counterfactual ΔP ≠ 0
Paired Wilcoxon signed-rank, P(no_X) vs P(original), on images with X present.

  vignette  (N=20):
    mean ΔP = +0.0070 [95% CI -0.0099, +0.0250]
    median ΔP = +0.0030
    Cohen's d (paired) = +0.174
    Wilcoxon W = 87.0, p = 0.5217
    H2-vignette supported? False

  ruler  (N=39):
    mean ΔP = +0.0030 [95% CI -0.0047, +0.0096]
    median ΔP = +0.0013
    Cohen's d (paired) = +0.130
    Wilcoxon W = 287.5, p = 0.1525
    H2-ruler supported? False

  hair (NC)  (N=220):
    mean ΔP = -0.0662 [95% CI -0.0837, -0.0486]
    median ΔP = -0.0479
    Cohen's d (paired) = -0.502
    Wilcoxon W = 5473.0, p = 0.0000
    H2-hair supported? True

  colorcast  (N=155):
    mean ΔP = +0.1039 [95% CI +0.0757, +0.1343]
    median ΔP = +0.0458
    Cohen's d (paired) = +0.536
    Wilcoxon W = 2625.0, p = 0.0000
    H2-colorcast supported? True

## H3 — cross-collection AUC gap decomposition
Compares per-collection AUC at original vs all_removed.

  c=212:
    AUC original    = 0.9644 [95% CI 0.9305, 0.9879]
    AUC all_removed = 0.8708 [95% CI 0.7983, 0.9308]
    ΔAUC            = -0.0936

  c=249:
    AUC original    = 0.7700 [95% CI 0.6707, 0.8571]
    AUC all_removed = 0.7060 [95% CI 0.6016, 0.8053]
    ΔAUC            = -0.0640

  c=70:
    AUC original    = 0.5300 [95% CI 0.4134, 0.6418]
    AUC all_removed = 0.7232 [95% CI 0.6188, 0.8165]
    ΔAUC            = +0.1932

  Gap (c=212 − c=70):
    original    = +0.4344
    all_removed = +0.1476
    closed by   = +0.2868 (+66.0%)
  H3 supported (≥ 30% gap closed)? True

## Primary Finding #1 — per-collection balanced AUC CIs
Bootstrap CIs on the prevalence-balanced AUCs (sanity for the slide-9 reframing).
  c=212: AUC = 0.9428 [95% CI 0.8953, 0.9790]
  c=249: AUC = 0.7776 [95% CI 0.6796, 0.8622]
  c=70: AUC = 0.5480 [95% CI 0.4316, 0.6626]

